  "lapsed_date": "09/12/2024",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall match those used in the existing building, unless otherwise shown on the approved drawings.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (Sustainability and Energy Statement, received 24/03/2021, Drawings 198/001(Rev.P1), 198/002(Rev.P1), 198/003(Rev.P1), 198/004(Rev.P1), 198/005(Rev.P1), 198/006(Rev.P1), 198/007(Rev.P1), 198/008(Rev.P1), 198/009(Rev.P1), 198/010(Rev.P1),198/011(Rev.P5), 198/012(Rev.P5), 198/013(Rev.P5), 198/014(Rev.P5), 198/015(Rev.P6), 198/016(Rev.P6), 198/017(Rev.P7), 198/018(Rev.P6), 198/019(Rev.P5), Design and Access Statement and Flood Risk Assessment, received 05/01/2021, and Photographs, received 29/01/2021) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, appropriate provisions for securing privacy to the private terraces at Units 1 and 2 (including screening and/or soft landscaping) shall have been submitted to for approval in writing by the Local Planning Authority, and the approved arrangements shall be installed and retained as such thereafter unless agreed otherwise with the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - Prior to first occupation of the development hereby approved, full details of the proposed ground floor cycle storage provision for unit 4 shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. Photographic evidence shall be submitted upon completion as verification and the approved provision shall be kept available thereafter at all times for the parking of bicycles.",
    "Condition : 7 - Prior to first occupation of the development hereby approved, evidence (including schedule of installed fittings and manufactures literature) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority to demonstrate that the development has achieved an internal water use of 105L/person/day or less.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to first use of the development, full details of the proposed arrangements for the storage and removal of waste and recycling (including the location and size of waste and recycling facilities) shall have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The development shall not be carried out otherwise than in accordance with the details thus approved.",
    "Condition : 9 - Before the development hereby permitted is first occupied or brought into use, the Local Planning Authority shall be informed of the agreed naming and numbering of the proposed dwellings so that arrangements can be put in place to ensure that, with the exception of a person eligible for a disabled person's badge issued pursuant to section 21 of the Chronically Sick and Disabled Persons Act 1970 (or similar legislation), no resident of the development shall obtain a resident's parking permit. Any occupiers of the approved development shall surrender any such permit wrongly issued or held.",
    "Condition : 10 - No new plumbing or pipes, other than rainwater pipes, shall be fixed to the external faces of buildings or associated structures."
  ],
